  "id": "Compound::DB00139 - Gene::10536",
  "verbalization": "Succinic Acid appears to interact with P3h2 and P3h1, both of which are involved in the catalytic activity of proline dioxygenase enzymes. This suggests a potential role for Succinic Acid in modulating the activity of these enzymes, which are critical in the synthesis of collagen. The evidence indicates that Succinic Acid binds to P3h2 and P3h1, and these proteins participate in the same biological process—proline dioxygenase activity—whose final product is linked to P3h3. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores supports a consistent mechanism where Succinic Acid influences the activity of these enzymes, ultimately affecting P3h3. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible regulatory role for Succinic Acid in the metabolic processes involving proline dioxygenase, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
